WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.316
Your organization's knowledge lives
in the tools your teams work in:

2
00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:08.774
wikis, documents, presentations,
chat threads, and more.

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:14.288
Your wire transfer cutoff policy is written
into documents across your organization.

4
00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:17.676
But when it changes, the
copies don't update together,

5
00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:21.637
so your teams and your AI can't
tell which one is current.

6
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:27.502
One out-of-date fact reaches your AI, your
support team, your contracts, and more.

7
00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:32.027
Your customers get the old answer, and
your teams spend their days correcting it.

8
00:00:32.027 --> 00:00:36.098
Now multiply that by all the
facts your organization runs on.

9
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.243
Arthos gives you one place for the
current answer: a trusted knowledge layer.

10
00:00:41.243 --> 00:00:46.489
Your tools stay as they are, and Arthos
pulls the facts out of them into that layer.

11
00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:49.140
Not everything written down is a fact.

12
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.567
Arthos is built to tell the difference:

13
00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:55.774
a decision from a discussion,
and a policy from a proposal.

14
00:00:56.917 --> 00:01:01.216
And as decisions change, Arthos
keeps each fact current.

15
00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:06.215
So your customers get the current answer,
your teams spend less time catching up,

16
00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:10.347
and your AI works from facts it
can trace back to the source.

17
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.608
Knowledge drifts.

18
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:14.040
Arthos catches it.

19
00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.909
Talk to us about keeping your
organization's knowledge current.

